{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "22",
   "text": "Will Trump's fiscal expansion undermine his goal of reducing the U.S. trade deficit?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "23",
   "text": "Tax cuts and spending increases boost U.S. demand",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "24",
   "text": "Fed model: import income elasticity around 2",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "25",
   "text": "Dollar moves take years to fully affect trade",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "26",
   "text": "Tax cuts and spending increases provide a large fiscal impulse",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#D1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "27",
   "text": "Simple model implies current-account deficit rises about 1% of GDP",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#D2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "28",
   "text": "Over half of the increase in domestic demand was spent abroad",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#D3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "29",
   "text": "Higher rates mechanically increase payments to foreign creditors",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#D4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "30",
   "text": "Euro and several Asian currencies were moving against the dollar",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#D5"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "31",
   "text": "Fiscal impulse adds roughly 50bp of GDP in imports over two years",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#D6"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "32",
   "text": "Stronger U.S. demand spills into foreign production",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "33",
   "text": "More income flows abroad on the U.S. debt stock",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "34",
   "text": "Exports rise and imports soften only after substantial lags",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "35",
   "text": "Import growth accelerates relative to the baseline",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "36",
   "text": "Higher interest payments add to the external deficit",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#C2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "37",
   "text": "Foreign growth and a softer dollar cannot offset the near-term impulse",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#C3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "38",
   "text": "U.S. fiscal stimulus boosts imports just as conditions were emerging for the trade deficit to improve",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "39",
   "text": "The U.S. is relatively closed and much of the tax cut may be saved",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "40",
   "text": "Historical income elasticities and trade relationships may not hold perfectly",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "41",
   "text": "Dollar depreciation and stronger foreign demand can improve U.S. trade",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "counterpoint",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_feb_15_18#R1"
  },
